OL,3,ACodebreaker, 103, kept his WW2 heroics
OL,4,Aa secret for decades
OL,5,
OL,6,F"My wife died and didn't know. I never
OL,7,Ftold anybody. In fact, she always
OL,8,Fcomplained - all your friends, when
OL,9,Fthey come visit, they all have stories
OL,10,Fto tell and you never tell anything."
OL,12,FFrom fleeing the Nazi invasion of his
OL,13,Fnative Poland, to training as an
OL,14,Foperative to work behind enemy lines,
OL,15,Fto helping to crack the codes which
OL,16,Fturned the tide of the conflict, Fred
OL,17,FVanke had an eventful World War Two.
OL,19,FSworn to secrecy however, his family
OL,20,Fand friends almost never learned of the
OL,21,Ftrue role the 103-year-old played in
OL,22,Fthe Allied war effort.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
